== pre-registered verdict (#256)
   ** class "hemco" has NO handles that dispatched prefetch: the AUC half of the rule cannot be
      evaluated for it, and "no separation" must NOT be concluded from its absence. **
   Spearman rho per class/arm (train on one arm, test on another — the agreed rule):
     mean_abs_gap_blocks     met/a=-0.866  met/b=-0.866  hemco=(no prefetching handles)   <- |rho|>=0.5 on 2+ arms (survives out-of-sample)
     max_abs_gap_blocks      met/a=-0.866  met/b=-0.866  hemco=(no prefetching handles)   <- |rho|>=0.5 on 2+ arms (survives out-of-sample)
     frac_large_gap          met/a=-1.000  met/b=-1.000  hemco=(no prefetching handles)   <- |rho|>=0.5 on 2+ arms (survives out-of-sample)
     mean_read_kib           met/a=n/a  met/b=n/a  hemco=(no prefetching handles)
     frac_monotonic          met/a=n/a  met/b=n/a  hemco=(no prefetching handles)
     frac_straddle           met/a=n/a  met/b=n/a  hemco=(no prefetching handles)

   best |rho| = 1.000 (frac_large_gap); threshold 0.5
   VERDICT: SEPARATION — a feature of a handle's first reads predicts byte follow-through.
